rumpy, uncooperative. A has leadership, anticipation, but unorganized, not good at criticism, show-off, not open to new ideas. C has reliability, positive crew atmosphere, quick decisions, calm, technical, but egocentric, communication difficulty, not willing to further education.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best fits overall. Perhaps C might be best because reliability and positive crew atmosphere are strong, plus calmness and quick decisions. The communication issues are concerning but maybe less severe than D's hot temper and know-it-all, and B's nasty remarks. A also has leadership but unorganized.\n\nThus as agent_1, we could argue that Candidate C emerges as the strongest overall, given 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions, calm under pressure, technical competence, and responsibility (maybe implied). While his communication issues are noted, they may be mitigated with training, and his reliability and crew atmosphere are critical.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: we can say we appreciate Agent 2's points but raise concerns about D's hot temper and know-it-all, which could jeopardize crew cooperation more than B's remarks. Also note that C's reliability and positive crew atmosphere are strong. Provide evidence: C known to be 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, keeps calm in crisis, can make correct decisions quickly. Also note his difficulty communicating and egocentric, but we can argue that his reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh.\n\nThus we may shift recommendation to C.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: \"C is known to be 100% reliable\", \"C creates a positive atmosphere with his crew\", \"C can make correct decisions quickly\", \"C keeps calm in a crisis\", \"C understands complicated technology\". Also mention his communication difficulty and egocentric as concerns.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE with recommendation for Candidate C, referencing prior contributions.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: {\"age